   "evidence": "Tietze.lean:161 `apply MonoidHom.toMulEquiv f g` with `PresentedGroup.ext` at :164/:168 mirrors the new :64-77. The checks `hf : \u2200 r \u2208 S, ((mk Q).comp \u03c3) r = 1` (:129) and `hg` (:136) have exactly the shape of the new `hu`/`hv`, and `h\u03b9\u03c3`/`h\u03c3\u03b9` (:118, :124) give the two recovery checks.",
   "file": "TauCeti/GroupTheory/Presentation/Tietze.lean",
   "fix": "Define `eliminateGenerators w R := equivOfGeneratorWords (Sum.elim FreeGroup.of w) (fun a \u21a6 FreeGroup.of (Sum.inl a)) hu hv hvu huv`. Get `hu` from the existing `hf`, `hv` from `hg`, `hvu` from `h\u03b9\u03c3` evaluated at `FreeGroup.of x`, and `huv` from `h\u03c3\u03b9` (which simp reduces to `rfl`). Then prove `eliminateGenerators_of_inl/_of_inr/_symm_of/_mk` by `equivOfGeneratorWords_of`/`_symm_of`/`_mk` plus `FreeGroup.lift_apply_of`, so the definition no longer needs to be unfolded with `simp [eliminateGenerators, MonoidHom.toMulEquiv]`.",
   "issue": "`eliminateGenerators` is `equivOfGeneratorWords` with forward words `Sum.elim FreeGroup.of w` and recovery words `FreeGroup.of \u2218 Sum.inl`, but it still builds the two maps itself and then uses `MonoidHom.toMulEquiv f g` with two `PresentedGroup.ext` checks (lines 140-168). This is the same skeleton as the new `equivOfGeneratorWords` (lines 55-77), so the file now has two parallel constructions.",
   "line": 110
  }
